53	\subsection{The Correlation-Selection Gap}
54	\label{sec:selection_gap}
55	
56	The gap has three layers: (1)~four instance-level signals cannot rank candidates by construction; (2)~MBR selection fails because degeneracy collapses the candidate pool; (3)~LP requires both low degeneracy and adequate alignment ($\rho \gtrsim 0.3$).
57	
58	\begin{table}[t]
59	\centering
60	\small
61	\caption{Best-of-$N$ NER selection (macro F1) on SciERC ($N{=}8$, $T{=}1.0$, 2-seed mean${\pm}\sigma$). LP is per-sample; others use consensus-proximity. Best non-oracle in \textbf{bold}. Non-tied subset in \S\ref{sec:discussion}; RE in Appendix~\ref{app:re_extension}.}
62	\label{tab:selection}
63	\begin{tabular}{lcc}
64	\toprule
65	Method & NER F1 & $p$ \\
66	\midrule
67	Oracle & $0.778 \pm 0.003$ & --- \\
68	Greedy ($T{=}0$) & $0.645 \pm 0.001$ & --- \\
69	\midrule
70	\multicolumn{3}{l}{\textit{Per-sample signal}} \\
71	LP           & $\mathbf{0.647} \pm 0.005$ & .29 \\
72	\midrule
